# Page Header

We use the `PageHeader` component across all learner-facing course pages, course administration pages, and platform administration pages.

## Course pages

- **Title**: the course title.
- **Breadcrumbs**: Home, Learn, Course Details, and the course page the user is on.
- **Back link**: leads to the course detail page.
- **Type**: `:slim`.

<%= embed Global::PageHeaderPreview, :course_page %>

### Course item pages

Item pages additionally render the `Items::Header` inside the page header, so the item the user is working on sits directly below the course it belongs to.

<%= embed Global::PageHeaderPreview, :course_item_page %>

### Course pages with navigation

The course details, forum, progress, and announcements pages show the course navigation instead of the title. Pass it as `navigation`: the header switches to the light accent background, and the title stays available to screen readers as the page heading.

<%= embed Global::PageHeaderPreview, :course_page_with_navigation %>

## Course administration

Course administration pages name the page itself as the header title, e.g. "Edit item", and carry the course they belong to as the `subtitle`. They show no breadcrumbs. Render them through the `course/shared/admin_page_header` partial rather than building the header per page.

<%= embed Global::PageHeaderPreview, :course_admin_page %>

## Platform administration

Platform administration pages show the page title with "Platform administration" as the `subtitle`.

<%= embed Global::PageHeaderPreview, :simple %>

## Additional content

Anything passed as content renders below the title, e.g. the course administration links.

<%= embed Global::PageHeaderPreview, :with_additional_content %>
